                                                                    46 1451
 Temperatures = 293.6 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 K.              46 1451
                                                                    46 1451
 History                                                            46 1451
 ----------                                                         46 1451
                                                                    46 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    46 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University. The inelastic     46 1451
 scattering cross section libraries for O in BeO were fully         46 1451
 developed using ab-initio and lattice dynamics methods [1]. Eight  46 1451
 temperatures are available in this library.  The LEAPR module      46 1451
 from NJOY code system was used to produce File 7, MT = 2, 4 data   46 1451
 for O in BeO as a mixed moderator.  Modifications to the LEAPR     46 1451
 source code were made to calculate the coherent elastic cross      46 1451
 section for O in BeO using the Debye Waller matrix method [2].     46 1451
 By convention, MAT=46 and ZA=146 are used for O in BeO.            46 1451
                                                                    46 1451
                                                                    46 1451
 Reference                                                          46 1451
 ----------                                                         46 1451
                                                                    46 1451
 1. A.I. Hawari, "Modern Techniques in Inelastic Thermal Neutron    46 1451
    Scattering Analysis," Nuclear Data Sheets 118 (2014) 172.       46 1451
 2. Y. Zhu, A. Hawari, "Implementation of a Generalized Coherent    46 1451
    Elastic Scattering Formulation for Thermal Neutron Scattering   46 1451
    Analysis", Proceedings of International Conference on Nuclear   46 1451
    Criticality Safety, Charlotte, NC, September 13-17, 2015.       46 1451
